      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I can confirm if the Head bone is the root transform of either a PhyBone or a converted DynamicBone script, it will indeed cause the issues. Even if the script is not directly on the head, as long as the Head is the root transform of said script, it will cause it.\nTo check for the issue is very simple as triggering the crouch or prone animation, and attempting to look up - the head will not tilt upward and still be facing towards the ground.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
